{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Out of the north comes gold</b> — He explained 'gold' as the brilliance of the sky, which resembles the appearance of gold, for from the direction of the north it begins to clear. And some say: the meaning of 'gold' is the wind, which is pure like gold; and the first is correct." "<b>And concerning God, terrible in majesty</b> — that one fears the majesty of the Place [i.e., God], at the sun's going forth, and human beings praise Him and rejoice."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:58.808073048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}